1
00:00:03,300 --> 00:00:12,388
For six years, her collar has told me where she sleeps, where she feeds, where she bathes. Tonight, it stopped moving.

2
00:00:13,800 --> 00:00:20,046
A rhino that stops moving at night is either asleep... or caught.

3
00:00:21,200 --> 00:00:27,642
Wire is cheap. A horn is worth a fortune.

4
00:00:28,600 --> 00:00:35,418
Three men. Three torches. And somewhere out there... her.

5
00:00:44,300 --> 00:00:51,882
Snares don't kill quickly. They hold. The harder she fights the wire, the deeper it cuts.

6
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:00,614
She doesn't run. She watches me decide.

7
00:01:16,200 --> 00:01:19,398
She could have crushed me. She didn't.

8
00:01:21,800 --> 00:01:24,412
The men who set the wire were coming back for her.

9
00:01:49,800 --> 00:01:53,013
They won't come back tonight.

10
00:01:55,600 --> 00:02:01,806
At first light, she does what her kind has always done.

11
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:12,418
Her forest is an island now. And the sea keeps rising.

12
00:02:13,800 --> 00:02:19,098
There may be fewer than fifty of them left.
